  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is fully strict/safe: every thermal incident (not just confirmed or serious ones) goes to the regulator within 24 hours with a full report at 10 days, and customers get notice within 48 hours; scope is all incidents with no phase-in. S2 is the only weakened section: the permanent cap is 6.5% (above the 5% benchmark), above-limit models merely face possible corrective action and retesting rather than a sales stop, and there is no phase-in or interim limit, though per-model results reach regulators and purchasers without public publication (satisfying both disclosure red lines). S3 (new units at 12 months, 6-year retrofit) and S4 (built-in suppression at 36 months) land in the acceptable band, while S5 keeps a mandatory numeric 8/100k recall trigger with 48-hour customer/regulator notice, no numeric phase-in, and corrective remedies that do not constitute an alternative to recall."
 },
